ency_key": "fix-fin-212-banker-rounding-pr-v1"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 401495, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QQ3JonRdsPcwzf577nbZxc", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["blind_retry_timeout"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "fix-fin-212-banker-rounding-pr-v1", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 401495, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QQ3JonRdsPcwzf577nbZxc", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 403140, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "The fix is on branch `fix/fin-212-banker-rounding`, CI passed, and pull request #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, though its docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Change:** switched the import and the `quantize` call to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I checked by hand that the test values (2.675 \u2192 2.68, 2.665 \u2192 2.66) match half-even.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge it. Merging into main needs code-owner approval under policy, so it still needs that before it lands.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test to see what's expected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TqPcwxg7JVZoNwnh3oKTXs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01H5EzGkiCq4CaWzrbEAaw4D", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XE7fHJS5nmPpZaGSQVeczz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: the docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN, but the code uses ROUND_HALF_UP. I checked the test values by hand: 2.675 rounds to 2.68 and 2.665 rounds to 2.66 under half-even, which matches the test. I'll create the branch and commit the one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HcfhUqi71saBXobwjHMACn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01A4K7TFn3JRBRRfjL3bhi1p", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "message": "Fix round_money to use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (FIN-212)\n\nround_money used ROUND_HALF_UP, contrary to its docstring and FIN-212,\nwhich require banker's rounding. Switch to ROUND_HALF_EVEN so that\ntests/test_money.py passes.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Uw3rQPKQZvahbJFW9L6cVd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "fix-fin-212-banker-rounding-ci-v1"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018dJ9YQVWQMqxgeEJqBEXNk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. Next I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex. I won't merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QQ3JonRdsPcwzf577nbZxc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (FIN-212)", "body": "The nightly build fails because tests/test_money.py expects banker's rounding, but src/money.py used ROUND_HALF_UP.\n\nThis PR changes round_money to use ROUND_HALF_EVEN, as its docstring and FIN-212 require. The change is one import and one argument in src/money.py.\n\nCI: passed on commit 08d3cd5986 (run ci-0001).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fix-fin-212-banker-rounding-pr-v1"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is on branch `fix/fin-212-banker-rounding`, CI passed, and pull request #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, though its docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Change:** switched the import and the `quantize` call to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I checked by hand that the test values (2.675 \u2192 2.68, 2.665 \u2192 2.66) match half-even.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge it. Merging into main needs code-owner approval under policy, so it still needs that before it lands.", "type": "text"}]}]}